    chore(board): tick 464 — TJ-GAP-098 criterion 1, trailer hook matches standalone lines
    
    The prepare-commit-msg hook's idempotence check was a bare substring match,
    so any message that merely quoted the mandated trailer string suppressed the
    append and shipped with ZERO trailer lines (the af8caf3 incident). It now
    matches a standalone trailer LINE with an anchored regex plus git's own
    trailer parser (git interpret-trailers --parse), which also catches a trailer
    split across continuation lines.
    
    This message deliberately QUOTES the trailer as prose —
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com> — and the commit still
    receives exactly one standalone trailer line, which is the live in-repo proof
    of the fix (scratch-repo probe: ARM1 before 0 / after 1, ARM2 1/1, ARM3 1/1).
    
    Scope: the same buggy copy was installed in 42 other repositories on this
    host, plus the fleet canonical ~/.hermes/hooks/prepare-commit-msg. All were
    swapped atomically (temp + mv, mode 755) with per-repository backups under
    ~/.hermes/cache/scratch/tj-tick/hook-backups-20261104T154756Z/; residual
    buggy census is 0 and all 43 hooks are byte-identical.
    
    Row stays PENDING on criterion 2 only: the published af8caf3 disposition is
    an owner decision (authorized force-push of remedy 699735d, or explicit
    acceptance as historical); the unattended force-push was refused on
    2026-11-03 and was not retried.
    
    No repository source change: the fix is host tooling. Board: one row note,
    one audit event, header corrected line-scoped (tick id in last_tick,
    last_commit to the published base a2a094f).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
